      "text": "2",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$f(x)=\\left(x^2+1\\right)\\left|x^2-a x+2\\right|+\\cos |x|$\n\nNotice that $\\cos (-x)=\\cos x=\\cos |x|$ which means $\\cos |x|$ is differentiable\neverywhere in $x \\in R$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Rightarrow f(x) \\text { can be non differentiable where }\\left|x^2-a x+2\\right| \\\\\n& =0\n\\end{aligned}$\n$\\Rightarrow x^2-a x+2=0$<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/J81bsNezDBmjuu9xkLrPJ_2cfOo9GqqgDXoHpc-FJdI.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n$\\Rightarrow 4-2 a+2=0 \\Rightarrow a=3$\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad\\left(x^2-3 x+2\\right)=0 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad x=1,2$\n$\\beta=1$\ndistance of $(\\alpha, \\beta)$ from line\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& 12 x+5 y+10=0 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\frac{|2(12)+5(1)+10|}{13}=\\frac{39}{13}=3\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
